 <sys:String x:Key="GuideTitle">QUICK GUIDE</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideDescription">How to use SW-MATE AI effectively</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideStep1">1. Open the Part/Assembly/Drawing you want to work with.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideStep2">2. Use AI CAD COMMAND to create, modify, or ask about the model.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideStep3">3. Review TASK PLAN; ✓ Verified means the Skill result was checked.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideStep4">4. Use MODEL INSPECTOR for a quick snapshot of actual CAD data.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideStep5">5. MANUAL CAD TOOLS are intended for testing and recovery.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideStep6">6. Ask about feature dependencies to see what depends on what and inspect design intent.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideStep7">7. For Assemblies, read the summary, components and mates before asking the Agent to modify the assembly.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideStep8">8. Insert/Move always uses Preview → Confirm; after execution you can Undo the last Agent action.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideStep9">9. AddMate uses two selected entities; ReplaceComponent also requires Preview/Confirm and supports Undo.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideStep10">10. DeleteMate runs only after Preview/Confirm and allows safe Undo only for supported Mate types.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideStep11">11. Assembly breakdown groups unique Parts, counts quantity and reads Part Number, Description, Material and finished size.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExamples">Example commands:</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExample1">• Create a 160 x 100 x 12 mm plate, two Ø12 holes, fillet R8</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExample2">• Change D1@Sketch1 to 70 mm</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExample3">• What is the current material?</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExample4">• What is the overall size?</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExample5">• What are the feature dependencies in this part?</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExample6">• If I change Boss-Extrude1, what features may be affected?</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExample7">• Summarize this Assembly.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExample8">• What components are in this Assembly?</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExample9">• What mates are in this Assembly?</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExample10">• Check interference in this Assembly.</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExample11">• Insert component &quot;E:\Models\Bracket.SLDPRT&quot; into Assembly at X=100, Y=0, Z=25 mm</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExample12">• Move component Bracket-1 to X=150, Y=20, Z=0 mm</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExample13">• Select two entities, then: Add coincident mate to selected entities</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExample14">• Replace component Bracket-1 with &quot;E:\Models\BracketV2.SLDPRT&quot;</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExample15">• Delete mate Coincident1</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideExample16">• Create a manufacturing breakdown for the current Assembly</sys:String>
 <sys:String x:Key="GuideTip">Tip: clearer dimensions, positions, and target objects help the Agent build a more accurate plan.</sys:String>
